{"_id":"6949661a3eeddc26d7c31b96","roadmapSlug":"django","nodeId":"AztOoGUtPW_6jP6NqJ5T-","description":"# Message Framework\n\nThe message framework in Django provides a way to deliver one-time notification messages, also known as \"flash messages,\" to users. These messages are typically used to provide feedback about the outcome of an action, such as a successful form submission or an error that occurred. They are stored temporarily and displayed to the user on their next page view, then automatically removed.","resources":[{"type":"official","title":"The messages framework","url":"https://docs.djangoproject.com/en/6.0/ref/contrib/messages/","_id":"6a7f4a75cb44947debcf70f0"},{"type":"article","title":"Messages Framework","url":"https://django-advanced-training.readthedocs.io/en/latest/features/contrib.messages/","_id":"6a7f4a75cb44947debcf70f1"},{"type":"article","title":"Implementing Messaging Functionality with the Messages Framework in Django","url":"https://medium.com/@iamalisaleh/implementing-messaging-functionality-with-the-messages-framework-in-django-23d7afc8f1d2","_id":"6a7f4a75cb44947debcf70f2"},{"type":"article","title":"Basics of Django Messages Framework","url":"https://micropyramid.com/blog/basics-of-django-message-framework/","_id":"6a7f4a75cb44947debcf70f3"},{"type":"video","title":"#23 Django tutorials | Passing Messages","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Mf_97YaUKag","_id":"6a7f4a75cb44947debcf70f4"},{"type":"video","title":"Exploring Django | The Messages Framework","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=MhUfgeWFgos","_id":"6a7f4a75cb44947debcf70f5"}],"createdAt":"2025-12-22T15:39:06.695Z","updatedAt":"2026-08-14T17:03:49.335Z","lessonPacks":[],"paidResources":[],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/django/content/AztOoGUtPW_6jP6NqJ5T-.md"}